00:04:50.417 --> 00:04:51.250
- So, Maks and Val,

00:04:51.250 --> 00:04:53.130
you're both born in
Odesa, Southern Ukraine

00:04:53.130 --> 00:04:55.380
and you now have a
nonprofit, helping Ukraine.

00:04:55.380 --> 00:04:57.030
So, can you tell us about that?

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.420
- We had no choice really.

00:04:58.420 --> 00:05:01.320
First of all, because
we're normal, good humans.

00:05:01.320 --> 00:05:03.300
We have great family values

00:05:03.300 --> 00:05:06.240
and we grew up with incredible parents.

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:08.640
But we're also first
generation immigrants.

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:09.750
We came from that place.

00:05:09.750 --> 00:05:10.593
It's our home.

00:05:11.580 --> 00:05:13.920
Our home became Brooklyn, New York

00:05:13.920 --> 00:05:17.010
in the nineties and have been
in United States ever since.

00:05:17.010 --> 00:05:19.770
But we are all from
somewhere in this place

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:23.760
and we value the values
that this country's on.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.520
And so, you know, the support that we show

00:05:26.520 --> 00:05:29.160
for Ukraine isn't just
because we're from there

00:05:29.160 --> 00:05:31.200
but also because those
people want this type

00:05:31.200 --> 00:05:32.580
of life and this type of lifestyle, so-

00:05:32.580 --> 00:05:36.336
- And because it's, it's
I think, in my opinion

00:05:36.336 --> 00:05:39.630
of how I view this country,
and the gratitude that I have

00:05:39.630 --> 00:05:41.371
for the United States for welcoming us

00:05:41.371 --> 00:05:44.220
I think it's the most
American thing to do.

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:45.053
- [Maks] Yep.

00:05:45.053 --> 00:05:46.140
- [Val] Is to help those that are in need.

00:05:46.140 --> 00:05:46.973
And so-

00:05:46.973 --> 00:05:47.806
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:47.806 --> 00:05:48.639
- [Val] Yeah.

00:05:48.639 --> 00:05:49.472
(audience clapping)

00:05:49.472 --> 00:05:50.610
- [Kelly] Agreed.

00:05:50.610 --> 00:05:52.020
I think it's really beautiful, too,

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.670
though, when you have
such a great spotlight

00:05:53.670 --> 00:05:54.660
and you have this support system,

00:05:54.660 --> 00:05:55.500
like this fan base,

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:56.940
and you use it for stuff like this.

00:05:56.940 --> 00:05:58.260
- We also wanna highlight that,

00:05:58.260 --> 00:05:59.370
on that video,

00:05:59.370 --> 00:06:00.780
most of the people that came,

00:06:00.780 --> 00:06:02.389
came without announcements.

00:06:02.389 --> 00:06:04.770
We didn't ask for anybody to come in.

00:06:04.770 --> 00:06:05.764
We just made a-

00:06:05.764 --> 00:06:07.920
made it known that this
is what we're doing.

00:06:07.920 --> 00:06:11.405
We're gathering humanitarian
aid for refugees,

00:06:11.405 --> 00:06:13.830
for people that have been displaced,

00:06:13.830 --> 00:06:14.820
first and foremost.

00:06:14.820 --> 00:06:17.700
And, you know, they have lived through

00:06:17.700 --> 00:06:18.870
the affects of this crazy-

00:06:18.870 --> 00:06:19.830
it's a war.

00:06:19.830 --> 00:06:22.260
It's the biggest since World War II,

00:06:22.260 --> 00:06:23.280
in my opinion.

00:06:23.280 --> 00:06:24.870
So, this was important for us.

00:06:24.870 --> 00:06:27.420
The people that came
from all walks of life

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:30.150
are hundreds and hundreds of volunteers

00:06:30.150 --> 00:06:31.020
that we never called,

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:34.590
and we're grateful for each
one, for every penny donated,

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.027
and we continue in our work.

00:06:36.027 --> 00:06:38.193
- You know, we talk about it-

00:06:39.086 --> 00:06:40.860
I think we're desensitized, almost,

00:06:40.860 --> 00:06:41.880
'cause we hear it so much.

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.890
But it's a crazy thing to
hear come out of your mouth.

00:06:43.890 --> 00:06:45.870
Like, someone being displaced,

00:06:45.870 --> 00:06:49.024
that is literally your life
has been ripped from you

00:06:49.024 --> 00:06:51.570
and you are put somewhere else.

00:06:51.570 --> 00:06:55.530
That has got to be the scariest
thing in the entire world.

00:06:55.530 --> 00:06:56.970
Like, not only just for an individual,

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.560
but especially if you're a parent.

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.790
How do you explain that to your kids?

00:06:59.790 --> 00:07:01.140
I can't even explain
the most simple things

00:07:01.140 --> 00:07:01.973
to my six and eight year old.

00:07:01.973 --> 00:07:02.806
I get-

00:07:02.806 --> 00:07:03.639
We just, we say it so much I think

00:07:03.639 --> 00:07:06.118
and we hear it so much in the
news that we get desensitized

00:07:06.118 --> 00:07:09.487
but it's, it's an incredibly sad thing.

00:07:09.487 --> 00:07:12.050
- Yeah. I think a lot of these
conversations get hijacked

00:07:12.050 --> 00:07:14.820
by politics and we're just treating it

00:07:14.820 --> 00:07:16.527
from the perspective of just humanity.

00:07:16.527 --> 00:07:17.360
- [Kelly] Basic humanity.

00:07:17.360 --> 00:07:18.193
- Yeah. I-

00:07:18.193 --> 00:07:20.970
We're not here to talk geopolitics.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:22.800
We're here to talk about human life being

00:07:22.800 --> 00:07:24.030
like you said, making-

00:07:24.030 --> 00:07:25.034
- Worth.

00:07:25.034 --> 00:07:25.867
- Being sacrificed. Yeah.

00:07:25.867 --> 00:07:28.740
- And also in, just for context, we

00:07:28.740 --> 00:07:32.070
are living in a generation
with the largest refugee crisis

00:07:32.070 --> 00:07:32.910
in the world.

00:07:32.910 --> 00:07:33.743
- [Maks] Absolutely.

00:07:33.743 --> 00:07:36.330
- Between Syria, between
Myanmar, between Ukraine

00:07:36.330 --> 00:07:39.570
there are the most amount of
displaced people internally

00:07:39.570 --> 00:07:41.307
in their countries and externally-

00:07:41.307 --> 00:07:42.140
